Constructs that open on one line and close on another. A reader standing at the first line end
sits inside each one, which is the position a region has to survive.

\parameters (
	size:"22pt"
	colour:"red"
)

\procedure spans-its-signature(
	a:"one"
	b:"""a triple-quoted value
carried to a second line"""
)
A body.
\end

<<spans-its-arguments a:"""an argument
carried across a line""">>

<$button class="a value
carried across a line">a double-quoted attribute</$button>

<$button class='a value
carried across a line'>a single-quoted attribute</$button>

<div>
<![CDATA[
a character-data payload across lines
]]>
</div>

<script>
/* a block comment
carried across lines */
var afterTheComment = 1; // a line comment
</script>
